      "content": "Double-quoted shell escaping also removes a backslash before `$` and backticks (and removes backslash-newline). This branch retains those backslashes, so a filter such as `--grep \"\\$\"` reaches Playwright as `\\$` instead of `$`, changing the regex and potentially the acceptance result. Handle these shell escape cases while continuing to treat the resulting characters as literal data; no evaluation is necessary.",
