    {
      "path": ".claude/scripts/acceptance-commands.sh",
      "content": "The parser accepts unterminated quotes and silently drops a trailing unquoted backslash. For example, `npm run test:unit -- 'foo` is converted to a valid `foo` filter and can pass this checker even though the documented command is syntactically incomplete. Detect an open quote or dangling escape, return a parsing error, and have the callers report `FAIL` rather than invoking the test-list command.",
